From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: qcom: q6asm-dai: undo the stream open when the format block fails

q6asm_dai_prepare() opens the ASM stream, maps the period buffers and
opens the COPP route before it sends the PCM media format (playback) or
encoder configuration (capture). When the DSP rejects that last command,
prepare only logged it (dev_info) and returned the error with the stream
still open, the buffers still mapped and the route still open, but with
the state not RUNNING. Neither the next prepare (it only closes a RUNNING
stream, then opens the same stream id again) nor close (same check)
undid it, so the DSP session stayed busy. Capture also queued its read
buffers on the failed stream.

Close the route, the stream and the mappings on that error like the
earlier error paths do, queue the capture buffers only after a
successful configuration, and log the failure as an error.

--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6asm-dai.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6asm-dai.c
@@ -298,19 +298,28 @@ static int q6asm_dai_prepare(struct snd_soc_component *component,
 							   runtime->rate,
 							   runtime->channels,
 							   prtd->bits_per_sample);
+	}
+	/*
+	 * A rejected format leaves the stream open, its buffers mapped and
+	 * the COPP routed while the state is not RUNNING, so neither the next
+	 * prepare nor close would undo it and the DSP session stays busy.
+	 */
+	if (ret < 0) {
+		dev_err(dev, "%s: CMD Format block failed: %d\n", __func__, ret);
+		goto format_err;
+	}
 
+	if (substream->stream == SNDRV_PCM_STREAM_CAPTURE) {
 		/* Queue the buffers */
 		for (i = 0; i < runtime->periods; i++)
 			q6asm_read(prtd->audio_client, prtd->stream_id);
-
 	}
-	if (ret < 0)
-		dev_info(dev, "%s: CMD Format block failed\n", __func__);
-	else
-		prtd->state = Q6ASM_STREAM_RUNNING;
+	prtd->state = Q6ASM_STREAM_RUNNING;
 
-	return ret;
+	return 0;
 
+format_err:
+	q6routing_stream_close(soc_prtd->dai_link->id, substream->stream);
 routing_err:
 	q6asm_cmd(prtd->audio_client, prtd->stream_id,  CMD_CLOSE);
 open_err:
